#{[17592186281324 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161784" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ca/ca49b92d602d04a73dc7ab9936d601654bd293ce3fb7950372ac86155875aca3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78eec2a4-7ee5-59eb-8402-37f965ae8bd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281324 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/00/0008ba406cfe8a5b61d683a6854260897cb441752a5333add281ab1279e31b0b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bbe6b6b897e5d53421080ae8e8b9dc49f2ea1b7e135f8426ee3f11af01cc2401.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}(2-\\frac{y}{3}+z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy & =[y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324184 #edb/ref 1080 "64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324184 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324184 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "187c8796-6dc3-5960-ad59-8f0656a81c13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324309 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324309 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324309 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2aa9da1c-2f67-5afd-a97d-d08f1c77a175" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324472 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324472 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324472 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3dfa63d1-2a3c-5f98-ac88-3e5a9c4a677a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324636 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324636 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324636 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "50f72eff-980c-5d6b-bc19-dfa625820604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324737 #edb/ref 1080 "72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324737 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324737 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c500570-ff2b-5461-8af9-215bc4a13b22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324827 #edb/ref 1080 "5\\sqrt{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324827 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324827 #edb/ref 1083