edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186527415 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186527670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186527718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186527752 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186527670 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527899 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e767016c-6faf-58ba-ac6e-34fede0af637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527910 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527821 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527910 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527910 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527910 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/57/5780b9e67272fdd78a24aab108fb9c672ee76ff2d62376991cea03c7efaa81fe.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527910 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00568ac8-b77a-5f52-9484-f19c655aa6d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527910 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/24/240cc6d74e266579aa848be820fd0014672aa0654f079c079472a896ad44c5fe.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y+2z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/27/27862dcc3effe5801c812f5c8944c0134d13bb38f99d337b0a4e20e9ff815639.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y+2z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{z}{12}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y+2z}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y+2z}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y+2z}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{z}{12}[x]_{x=0}^{x=4-y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{z}{12}(4-y+2z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(4z-yz+2{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(4z-yz+2{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(4z-yz+2{z}^{2})\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{12}{[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{12}(18-\\frac{9}{2}y+18)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(3-\\frac{3}{8}y)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(3-\\frac{3}{8}y)\\,dy & ={[3y-\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4} \\\\  & =(12-3)-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527912 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527912 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{y+z}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0884b1e2-1bba-5f2c-8a6a-f7af258e16fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527912 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{y+z}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=y}^{x=y+z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[y{z}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(16-1) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527947 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527947 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527947 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527947 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,(3y-z)^{2}\\le x\\le {e}^{y+4z}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527947 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5bfcca82-6474-54bc-a5e0-2e4323bbf96b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527947 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=(3y-z)^{2}\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={e}^{y+4z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527982 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527982 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161578" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527982 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527982 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y-z\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527982 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b38931ca-6fb1-5b3c-b019-b45d2fe482a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527982 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[2x]_{x=0}^{x=4-y-z}dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2(4-y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[8z-2yz-{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-1\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}7-2y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}7-2y\\,dy & ={[7y-{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =7-1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527988 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161572" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527988 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527988 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y-z}24y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527988 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf9108b7-225d-5060-8e6a-417eee5fc631" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527988 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y-z}24y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}24y[x]_{x=0}^{x=1-y-z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24y(1-y-z)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24y-24{y}^{2}-24yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}24y-24{y}^{2}-24yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}24(y-{y}^{2})-24yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24(y-{y}^{2})[z]_{z=0}^{z=y}-12y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24(y-{y}^{2})y-12{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24{y}^{2}-36{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8{y}^{3}-9{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1/2} \\\\  & =8(\\frac{1}{8}-0)-9(\\frac{1}{16}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527997 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527997 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161562" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527997 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527997 #edb/ref 1071 "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le z,\\,2\\le z\\le 3,\\,-y-z\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+{z}^{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527997 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d3a2b2c0-5dc8-56bd-94aa-3a2ccfd9aff3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186527997 #edb/ref 1074 "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a9/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-y-z,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={y}^{2}+{z}^{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le z,\\,2\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{z}[{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{z}{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=-2+z=z-2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528005 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528005 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528005 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528005 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xyz\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le y+z\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the line $z=y$ in the first quadrant." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528005 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e31a3154-dd92-51e0-baa5-7e556d0b4865" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528005 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xyz\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}yz[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=y+z}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz(y+z)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz({y}^{2}+2yz+{z}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/59/5974f852ba8dcaf9e6c4d6323709987c590e2f739524e012545738bc4bb842b0.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}{z}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}y{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}y\\cdot {y}^{4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{17}{12}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}{[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}(\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528011 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186527899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528011 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161690" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528011 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528011 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ca/ca994203c4a3889949e3452f48ea3f7295a152c5d9d4c809758f152d7115cedf.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528011 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f2d33e33-cbe1-5877-8ed6-72bcb8e7fff5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186528011 #edb/ref 1074 "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=2.$\n\n![](images/a3/a39d7a27f20283b6e6814db926801f16e3e2cb42c7fe16487350b536d3b63d3c.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-(y-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](images/50/5058493860a1c4d919e3cd6786bb1aca156ae83d47f766c087e351e9764929c4.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-(y-1)^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z[{x}^{2}]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
